.TH DDN-FIXUP "1" "2026\-11\-25" "ddnetmirror 1.0.0" "ddnetmirror manual"
.SH NAME
ddn fixup \- apply text fixup rules to a copy of a config file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ddn
fixup [-h] [--verbose] (input --rules RULES --output OUTPUT | --check RULES)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apply text fixup rules to a copy of a config file. The input is never modified; the output is a new file.

.TP
\fBinput\fR
config file to read (UTF\-8)

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rules\fR \fI\,RULES\/\fR
YAML rule file

.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR
new output file; never overwritten

.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
also name what each rule changed (blocks, fragments, separator runs); never
prints config text

.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR \fI\,RULES\/\fR
only validate a rule file: reads no config and writes nothing

.SH DISTRIBUTION
The latest version of ddnetmirror may be downloaded from
.UR https://github.com/DaphnisDuck/ddnetmirror
.UE
